@SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5000
### Change to your host address ^


###=====================================Login (run this first)=====================================
### Register and login share the "public" rate-limiting policy with the repair
### endpoints below (10 requests/minute per IP by default); a 429 here just means
### you ran this file too many times in a row.

### Register a worker account (skip if you already have one)
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "worker1",
  "email": "worker1@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Log in. REST Client's "named request" feature lets @token below read
### the token straight out of this response, so it never has to be pasted
### or committed anywhere.
# @name login
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "worker1",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}


###=====================================List of Product requests=====================================

### Product catalogue (anonymous; the customer app builds its repair form from this)
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/products
Accept: application/json


###=====================================List of Repair requests=====================================

### List of all repairs
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs?page=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a repair (anonymous, rate limited; product name must exist in GET /api/products
### unless isCustomProduct is true)
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product": "Monitor interaktywny myBoard Titan (Android 15)",
  "isCustomProduct": false,
  "serialNumber": "L241001056512345",
  "description": "Broken screen",
  "reporterName": "Jan",
  "reporterSurname": "Kowalski",
  "reporterPhone": "123456789",
  "reporterEmail": "jan@example.com",
  "companyName": "Example sp. z o.o.",
  "companyAddress": "Example 1",
  "companyPostalCode": "00-001",
  "companyCity": "Warszawa",
  "companyNip": "1234563218",
  "hasWarranty": false,
  "hasContract": false,
  "serviceDataConsent": true,
  "marketingConsent": false
}


### Check repair status (anonymous, rate limited; email is matched case-insensitively)
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/check
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 1,
  "email": "jan@example.com"
}


### Assign the current user to a pending repair
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/18/take
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Complete a repair that is in progress
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/18/complete
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Cancel a repair
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/21/cancel
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Return an in-progress repair to the pending queue
POST {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/22/return
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Edit repair data (status is not part of this DTO, use PUT .../status below)
### isCustomProduct: true means the product is not in GET /api/products,
### so the serial number is optional and not format-checked.
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/17
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "product": "Ekran dotykowy - inny model",
  "isCustomProduct": true,
  "serialNumber": "SN-12345",
  "description": "Screen completely shattered",
  "reporterName": "Jan",
  "reporterSurname": "Kowalski",
  "reporterPhone": "123456789",
  "reporterEmail": "jan@example.com",
  "companyName": "Example sp. z o.o.",
  "companyAddress": "Example 2",
  "companyPostalCode": "00-002",
  "companyCity": "Warszawa",
  "companyNip": "1234563218",
  "hasWarranty": false,
  "hasContract": false
}


### Correct a repair's status (Admin role only; only specific transitions are allowed,
### e.g. Pending -> Cancelled, see README)
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/17/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "status": "Cancelled"
}


### Delete repair with id ...
DELETE {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/repairs/20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


###=====================================List of User requests=====================================

### List of all users
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Selected user
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/17
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Logged user
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/logged
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update user
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/13
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "username": "john76",
  "email": "john67@example.com"
}

### Change own password
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "currentPassword": "Password123!",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword456!"
}

### Delete user
DELETE {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/9
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Grant / revoke permissions
# ===========================
# All permissions:
#   ReadRepairs, TakeRepairs, EditRepairs, DeleteRepairs,
#   ReadUsers, EditUsers, DeleteUsers, GrantUsers, DischargeUsers
# ===========================
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/grant/17
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "permissionsGranted": [
    "ReadRepairs",
    "TakeRepairs"
  ],
  "permissionsRevoked": []
}


###=====================================List of Admin management requests=====================================

### List admins, ordered by priority (Admin only)
GET {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/admins
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Promote a worker to admin (Admin only)
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/13/promote-admin
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change an admin's priority; lower number = more authority (Admin only)
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/13/priority
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "priority": 2
}

### Demote an admin back to worker (Admin only)
PUT {{SerwisSystem_Api_HostAddress}}/api/users/13/demote-admin
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
